From 94399d9ad7fb2aa78adb0085ca27f4179ace3d5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valentin Churavy <v.churavy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:27:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give the loop vectorizer the vector math library of CPU
 codegen

With ENABLE_HOST_CPU_VECTORIZE_{LIBMVEC,SLEEF,SVML}, only codegen's
TargetLibraryInfo knows about the vector math library: it maps vectorized
calls to math intrinsics to the library there (ReplaceWithVeclib). The
optimization pipeline, which runs InjectTLIMappings and LoopVectorize, uses
the default TargetLibraryInfo without any vector functions. So the loop
vectorizer's cost model sees every vector math call as scalarized (four
scalar calls plus inserts and extracts at width 4) and the vector loop costs
about as much as the scalar one. Whether a kernel vectorizes then depends on
the arithmetic around the calls: on x86-64 AVX2, log(x)+exp(x)+sin(x)+cos(x)
stays scalar while log(x)+exp(x)+sin(x)+cos(2x) vectorizes, and kernels with
several math calls and little other arithmetic fall back to scalar libm.

Build the vector library's TargetLibraryInfoImpl in one place and register
it for the optimization pipeline too, both in PoCLModulePassManager and in
the separate pipeline populateModulePM runs. LoopVectorize now costs the
real vector variants and calls them directly.

LoopVectorize does not check a variant's ISA, or whether the library
exports it, before calling it. It calls libmvec's AVX2 variants from SSE and
AVX targets (SIGILL with SLEEF's gnuabi library, which has no dispatch;
wrong arguments with an SSE caller), SVML's AVX-512 variants from AVX2
targets, and SVE variants on SVE targets that SLEEF builds without SVE
lack. So the optimization pipeline only gets the table when the device CPU
can call every variant the vectorizer may pick: libmvec on x86 with AVX2,
SVML with AVX-512F, SLEEF on AArch64 without SVE. Other targets keep the
codegen-only mapping.

Measured on Zen 3 (AVX2, the SLEEF gnuabi build reached through the libmvec
table), one thread, ns per element:

  kernel                     Float64        Float32
  log+exp+sin*cos            21.2 ->  7.1   15.6 -> 2.9
  log+exp+sin*cos+pow        75.9 -> 15.4   66.8 -> 7.1
  log+exp+sin+cos+tan        32.7 ->  9.2   17.5 -> 4.2

Kernels that already vectorized are unchanged. Loops that newly vectorize
call the library's vector variants instead of scalar libm, so their results
can differ by a few ulp, as for kernels that vectorized before.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Opus 5.5)
---
 examples/vecbuiltin/vecbuiltin.fc |  46 +++++++------
 lib/CL/pocl_llvm_api.h            |   9 ++-
 lib/CL/pocl_llvm_wg.cc            | 103 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 111 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

diff --git a/examples/vecbuiltin/vecbuiltin.fc b/examples/vecbuiltin/vecbuiltin.fc
index 2442fc6f..4204f42c 100644
--- a/examples/vecbuiltin/vecbuiltin.fc
+++ b/examples/vecbuiltin/vecbuiltin.fc
@@ -1,22 +1,28 @@
 # test autovectorization of builtins
+#
+# With a vector math library, the loop vectorizer may call its vector
+# variants (_ZGV* for libmvec and SLEEF, __svml_* for SVML) directly
+# instead of emitting vector intrinsics; a call of either means the builtin
+# was vectorized. (Vector library declarations alone don't: they are added
+# even when the calls stay scalar.)
 
-# CHECK: llvm.sin.v
-# CHECK: llvm.cos.v
-# CHECK: llvm.log2.v
-# CHECK: llvm.pow.v
-# CHECK: llvm.exp.v
-# CHECK: llvm.exp2.v
-# CHECK: llvm.fabs.v
-# CHECK: llvm.fma.v
-# CHECK: llvm.maxnum.v
-# CHECK: llvm.minnum.v
-# CHECK: llvm.log10.v
-# CHECK: llvm.log.v
-# CHECK: llvm.rint.v
-# CHECK: llvm.round.v
-# CHECK: llvm.sqrt.v
-# CHECK: llvm.ceil.v
-# CHECK: llvm.tan.v
-# CHECK: llvm.powi.v
-# CHECK: llvm.floor.v
-# CHECK: llvm.trunc.v
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.sin\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_sinf\(|@__svml_sinf[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.cos\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_cosf\(|@__svml_cosf[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.log2\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_log2f\(|@__svml_log2f[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.pow\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_powf\(|@__svml_powf[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.exp\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_expf\(|@__svml_expf[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.exp2\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_exp2f\(|@__svml_exp2f[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.fabs.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.fma.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.maxnum.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.minnum.v
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.log10\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_log10f\(|@__svml_log10f[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.log\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_logf\(|@__svml_logf[0-9]+\(}}
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.rint.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.round.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.sqrt.v
+# CHECK-DAG: llvm.ceil.v
+# CHECK-DAG: call {{.*}}{{@llvm\.tan\.v|@_ZGV[A-Za-z0-9]+_tanf\(|@__svml_tanf[0-9]+\(}}
